course: dictionary
lesson: 16087
title: Washed and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word washed has more than one meaning, so use the words around it to find the right one. «I washed my hands with soap before lunch.» Here washed means made clean with water. The words hands, soap and before lunch are the clues.
explain: Washed can also mean carried along by water. «The waves washed the shells up onto the sand.» The waves are doing the moving, so washed means carried in by the water. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases change the meaning completely. «After the storm, the picnic was washed out.» Washed out here means cancelled because of rain, not clean. Phrases like washed away and washed up have their own meanings too, so read the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: Washed is the past form of wash: wash, washes, washed, washing.
fact: Washed means made clean with water, often with soap.
fact: Washed also means carried along by water or waves, as in «washed up on the beach».
fact: Washed out means pale and tired, or, for a game, cancelled because of rain.
fact: Washed up (informal) means no longer successful. Informal means a relaxed, everyday way of speaking.
exercise: «I washed my hands with soap before lunch.» What does washed mean here? | Cancelled because of rain | Pale and tired | Carried along by waves | *Made clean with water and soap
exercise: «The waves washed the shells up onto the sand.» What brought the shells onto the beach? | A child with a bucket | A bird flying over the sea | A dog running along the sand | *The waves
exercise: «After the storm, the picnic was washed out.» What does washed out mean here? | Hungry | Made clean | *Cancelled because of rain | Very loud
test: «Freshly washed fruit tastes best.» What does freshly washed mean? | *Clean, because it has just been rinsed with water | Old and dusty | Pale and tired | Carried away by a river
test: Why should fruit and vegetables be washed before we eat them? | *To remove dirt before we eat them | To make them go bad | Because they must be cooked first | To make them louder
exam: Sam says, «The old pop star is washed up now.» What does washed up mean here? | Found on the beach | Cancelled because of rain | Cleaned with soap | *No longer successful
